r@noaa.gov", "senderName": "NWS Paducah KY", "headline": "Extreme Heat Warning issued July 28 at 11:19AM CDT until July 28 at 7:00PM CDT by NWS Paducah KY", "description": "* WHAT...Dangerously hot conditions with heat index values up to 113.\n\n* WHERE...Portions of southern Illinois, western Kentucky, and\nsoutheast Missouri.\n\n* WHEN...Until 7 PM CDT this evening.\n\n* IMPACTS...Heat related illnesses increase significantly during\nextreme heat and high humidity events.", "instruction": "Drink plenty of fluids, stay in an air-conditioned room, stay out of\nthe sun, and check up on relatives and neighbors.\n\nTake extra precautions when outside. Wear lightweight and loose\nfitting clothing. Try to limit strenuous activities to early morning\nor evening. Take action when you see symptoms of heat exhaustion and\nheat stroke.\n\nTo reduce risk during outdoor work, the Occupational Safety and\nHealth Administration recommends scheduling frequent rest breaks in\nshaded or air conditioned environments. Anyone overcome by heat\nshould be moved to a cool and shaded location. Heat stroke is an\nemergency! Call 9 1 1.", "response": "Execute", "note": null, "parameters": {"AWIPSidentifier": ["NPWPAH"], "WMOidentifier": ["WWUS73 KPAH 281619"], "NWSheadline": ["EXTREME HEAT WARNING REMAINS IN EFFECT UNTIL 7 PM CDT THIS EVENING"], "BLOCKCHANNEL": ["EAS", "NWEM", "CMAS"], "VTEC": ["/O.CON.KPAH.XH.W.0003.000000T0000Z-260729T0000Z/"], "eventEndingTime": ["2026-07-28T19:00:00-05:00"], "expiredReferences": ["w-nws.webmaster@noaa.gov,urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.78be5ae073ca888bbfa03f8fca88e2c40d672aa7.003.1,2026-07-27T11:28:00-05:00 w-nws.webmaster@noaa.gov,urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.3abcca12cbb147ac87fd4b9be7bf0554c2e0074b.002.1,2026-07-27T00:32:00-05:00 w-nws.webmaster@noaa.gov,urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.181c481223c04ba871c8184011044a6526132ad2.002.1,2026-07-27T00:24:00-05:00 w-nws.webmaster@noaa.gov,urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.6b61695d8a7a42f9795d038e02e99c5b1a4d655a.002.2,2026-07-26T09:13:00-05:0